\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":99,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser ad-free books-on-film\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"39243\",\"name\":\"GIANT - The Play\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"giant---the-play\",\"posterImage\":\"7ogw155b615n9fsgkymx9oqc11hw\",\"bannerImage\":\"kxglnu5t5y1j72btf35s2bi3y6mt\",\"synopsis\":\"\\u003cp class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin: 0cm; line-height: 16.8667px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-align: justify;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eGIANT, the 5-star critically acclaimed play starring John Lithgow (\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003ci style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eKillers of the Flower Moon\\u003c/i\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003e, \\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003ci style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eThe Crown\\u003c/i\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003e) as Roald Dahl, comes to the big screen. Winner of 3 Olivier Awards® including Best Play and a Tony Award® for Best Actor in a Play (John Lithgow), the production was filmed live in London’s West End ahead of its sold-out Broadway run. The stellar cast includes Aya Cash (\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003ci style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eThe Boys, The Franchise, \\u003cspan style=\\\"color: rgb(49, 49, 49);\\\"\\u003eYou’re the Worst\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/i\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(49, 49, 49);\\\"\\u003e)\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003e, Elliot Levey (\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003ci style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eCold War, Patriots, Good\\u003c/i\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003e) and Rachael Stirling (\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003ci style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003eThe Divine Mrs S\\u003c/i\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\\\"\\u003e).\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin: 0cm; line-height: 16.8667px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\\\"\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"margin: 0cm; line-height: 16.8667px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\\\"\\u003eA world-famous children’s author under threat. A battle of wills in the wake of scandal. And one chance to make amends...It’s the summer of 1983, \\u003ci\\u003eThe Witches\\u003c/i\\u003e is about to hit the shelves and Roald Dahl is making last-minute edits.\\u0026nbsp; But the outcry at his recent, explicitly antisemitic article won’t die down. Across a single afternoon at his family home, and rocked by an unexpectedly explosive confrontation, Dahl is forced to choose: make a public apology or risk his name and reputation. Inspired by real events,\\u003cb\\u003e \\u003c/b\\u003eGIANT\\u003ci\\u003e \\u003c/i\\u003eexplores with dark humour the difference between considered opinion and dangerous rhetoric offering a complicated portrait of a fiendishly charismatic icon.\\u003co:p\\u003e\\u003c/o:p\\u003e\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"starring\":\"John Lithgow, Aya Cash, Elliot Levey, Rachael Stirling\",\"directedBy\":\"Nicholas Hytner\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":136,\"genre\":\"\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":null,\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-11-19\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-11-19\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"515213\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Giant - the play (theatre) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99312099994,\\\"daysShown\\\":133,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-event-cinema some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-event-cinema every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-event-cinema showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"460371\",\"time\":\"2026-11-19T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":9,\"screenId\":\"439\",\"seatsRemaining\":116,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"460372\",\"time\":\"2026-11-22T16:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":3,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":98,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"460373\",\"time\":\"2026-11-30T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":6,\"screenId\":\"439\",\"seatsRemaining\":119,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"460374\",\"time\":\"2026-12-02T13:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":101,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"35440\",\"name\":\"The Killers\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-killers\",\"posterImage\":\"719nlc7jes4f37yrgdrkboxzbk53\",\"bannerImage\":\"zmfonzp60mj3kuu51rvaczfevx74\",\"synopsis\":\"Local film critic and podcaster Matthew Turner returns for a third mini season of film noir classics, which will run exclusively at Chiswick Cinema throughout November 2026.\\n\\n\\\"Along with Double Indemnity and Sunset Boulevard, Robert Siodmak's crime thriller has one of the all-time great noir opening scenes, as a pair of gun-toting killers arrive in a small town and execute The Swede (Burt Lancaster), who makes no effort to resist his own death. Flashbacks then reveal what lead him to this state, including a doomed dalliance with femme fatale Kitty Collins (Ava Gardner, at her sultriest).\\\"\\n\\nSynopsis:\\nTwo hit men walk into a diner asking for a man called \\\"the Swede\\\" (Burt Lancaster). When the killers find the Swede, he's expecting them and doesn't put up a fight. Since the Swede had a life insurance policy, an investigator (Edmond O'Brien), on a hunch, decides to look into the murder. As the Swede's past is laid bare, it comes to light that he was in love with a beautiful woman (Ava Gardner) who may have lured him into pulling off a bank robbery overseen by another man (Albert Dekker).\",\"starring\":\"Ava Gardner, Burt Lancaster, Edmond O'Brien, Sam Leverne\",\"directedBy\":\"Robert Siodmak\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":105,\"genre\":\"Thriller\",\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cq_gxqCaFms\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-11-25\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-11-25\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"484879\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"#Runseokjin_Ep.Tour The Movie (Concert) [12A]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99312699994,\\\"daysShown\\\":126,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Noirvember\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Noirvember\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-intro some-showings-ad-free some-showings-noirvember every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-intro every-showings-ad-free every-showings-noirvember showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"406311\",\"time\":\"2026-11-25T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":0,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":101,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser intro ad-free noirvember\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"34355\",\"name\":\"Back To The Future\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"back-to-the-future-40th-anniversary\",\"posterImage\":\"r704nxzmjirzi1vzrksx66m6wso5\",\"bannerImage\":\"sydxwbbnpp7wpr46z739qbazj5m5\",\"synopsis\":\"Dive into film history and technique with handpicked classics. A friendly introduction and a post-film sociable discussion with film-maker Andrea Carnevali.\\n\\nAcademy Award Wins Best Effects\\nAcademy Award Nominations Best Song, Best Sound, Best Screenplay\\n\\nEighties teenager Marty McFly is accidentally sent back in time to 1955, inadvertently disrupting his parents' first meeting and attracting his mother's romantic interest. Marty must repair the damage to history by rekindling his parents' romance and - with the help of his eccentric inventor friend Doc Brown - return to 1985.\",\"starring\":\"Michael J. Fox, Christopher Lloyd, Crispin Glover\",\"directedBy\":\"Robert Zemeckis\",\"producedBy\":\"Bob Gale, Neil Canton\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":116,\"genre\":\"Adventure\",\"allGenres\":\"Adventure, Comedy, Science Fiction\",\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"ez6WQ7IX72U\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2025-10-31\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-11-26\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":22.0787,\"tmdbId\":\"105\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"2196538\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Back To The Future (40Th Anniversary) [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99312799994,\\\"daysShown\\\":127,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Andrea's Film Club\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Andrea's Film Club\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-intro some-showings-ad-free some-showings-andreas-film-club every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-intro every-showings-ad-free every-showings-andreas-film-club showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"394982\",\"time\":\"2026-11-26T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":10,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":91,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser intro ad-free andreas-film-club\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"39825\",\"name\":\"Case 137 [Dossier 137]\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"case-137-dossier-137\",\"posterImage\":\"9o0irwz8tgesdl4tjnuzhelomno2\",\"bannerImage\":\"nv80culwthqohc8aph16lmasxb4e\",\"synopsis\":\"File 137 is apparently one more case for Stéphanie, an investigator at the IGPN, the police force. A tense demonstration, a young man injured by a shot from LBD, circumstances to be clarified to establish responsibility. But an unexpected element will trouble Stéphanie, for whom file 137 becomes something other than a simple number.\",\"starring\":null,\"directedBy\":null,\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":116,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"DRKJKfGbEjc\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-11-28\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-11-28\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"463862\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"CASE 137 (2D) [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"410\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99312999994,\\\"daysShown\\\":129,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"French Impressions\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"French Impressions\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-films some-showings-intro some-showings-ad-free some-showings-french-impressions every-showings-intro every-showings-ad-free every-showings-french-impressions showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"466811\",\"time\":\"2026-11-28T11:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":1,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":100,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"intro ad-free french-impressions\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"39064\",\"name\":\"Chimes at Midnight\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"chimes-at-midnight\",\"posterImage\":\"4zfrg7cu2ojqer9lsjpoh1bwm86n\",\"bannerImage\":\"fieztqgcdz057mqtv047p4jktjxs\",\"synopsis\":\"\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cdiv style=\\\"\\\"\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003eDirected by and starring Orson Welles with John\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003eGielgud, Keith Baxter and Jeanne Moreau. One of the finest Shakespeare films ever made and one of Welles's supreme achievements, this distillation of the two parts of Henry 1V sees Falstaff's decline and fall as a symbol of the death of Merrie England.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003eAbout the season:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003ePeople often say that if Shakespeare were alive today he would be writing for the movies. What is startling is how often, since the beginnings of cinema, his plays have been adapted for the screen.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003eFollowing a highly successful season devoted to the work of Harold Pinter, Chiswick Cinema now focuses on the infinite variety of filmed Shakespeare and will accompany four major screenings with talks, supplementary showings and celebrity interviews.\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\",\"starring\":\"Orson Welles, Jeanne Moreau, Margaret Rutherford, John Gielgud, Marina Vladywalter Chiari\",\"directedBy\":\"Orson Welles\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":116,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"bxdJTgBHqUQ\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-11-29\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-11-29\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"39874\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Chimes At Midnight (Re: 2015) (2D) [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99313099994,\\\"daysShown\\\":130,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Q\\\\u0026A\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Shakespeare on Screen\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Q\\\\u0026A\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Shakespeare on Screen\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-qa some-showings-intro some-showings-shakespeare-on-screen every-showings-qa every-showings-intro every-showings-shakespeare-on-screen showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"465462\",\"time\":\"2026-11-29T19:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":2,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":99,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"qa intro shakespeare-on-screen\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"37997\",\"name\":\"The Royal Ballet: The Nutcracker\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-royal-ballet-the-nutcracker-2\",\"posterImage\":\"u8sjafpos71qx2gfk9nwefvfbzzf\",\"bannerImage\":\"7towl7taq2x98ul0bi4ua23zb2jp\",\"synopsis\":\"\\u003cdiv\\u003eAt a cosy Christmas party, young Clara meets the mysterious magician Drosselmeyer, who gives her a nutcracker doll. When the guests have departed and the house is asleep, Clara sneaks downstairs in search of the doll. Instead, she finds Drosselmeyer, who whisks her away on a journey into a whole world of enchantment: fantastical landscapes of flurried snow and glittering confection where toys come alive and the magic never stops.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003ePeter Wright’s production of this festive family favourite sparkles to the wondrous swell of Tchaikovsky’s orchestral score, alongside the glow and grandeur of Julia Trevelyan Oman’s period designs.\\u003c/div\\u003e\",\"starring\":\"Mayara Magri, Reece Clarke, James Hay, Marianna Tsembenhoi, Taisuke Nakao\",\"directedBy\":\"Peter Wright\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":140,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"eRR1FiG__FU\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-12-01\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-12-01\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"500517\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Nutcracker 2025 - Rbo, London 2026 (Ballet), The [Unknown]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99313299994,\\\"daysShown\\\":147,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-event-cinema some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-event-cinema every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-event-cinema showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"442093\",\"time\":\"2026-12-01T19:15:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":6,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":95,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"442094\",\"time\":\"2026-12-16T16:35:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":2,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":99,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"38105\",\"name\":\"The Metropolitan Opera: Samson et Dalila\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"the-metropolitan-opera-samson-et-dalila\",\"posterImage\":\"ihk556kut228f15iu3tpoltay9x7\",\"bannerImage\":\"c8wvbok7yhr77syk4va78y6886kz\",\"synopsis\":\"\\u003cdiv\\u003eSaint-Saëns’s spectacular take on the biblical hero of legendary strength and the seductive Philistine whose beauty overpowers him returns in the Met’s larger-than-life production. Featuring a massive orchestra and chorus and some of opera’s most spellbinding tunes, this masterpiece is a feast for the eyes and ears. Giacomo Sagripanti conducts an electrifying cast led by the formidable star pairing of mezzo-soprano Aigul Akhmetshina and tenor Clay Hilley, broadcast live to cinemas worldwide.\\u003c/div\\u003e\",\"starring\":\"Aigul Akhmetshina, Clay Hilley\",\"directedBy\":null,\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":234,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"TBC\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":null,\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-12-05\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-12-05\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"484879\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"#Runseokjin_Ep.Tour The Movie (Concert) [12A]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"411\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99313699994,\\\"daysShown\\\":140,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Event Cinema\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-event-cinema some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-event-cinema every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-event-cinema showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"441993\",\"time\":\"2026-12-05T17:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":10,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":91,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"},{\"id\":\"441994\",\"time\":\"2026-12-09T11:30:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":4,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":97,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser event-cinema\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"39374\",\"name\":\"Phantom Thread\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"phantom-thread\",\"posterImage\":\"ngqls631d2pa6uen1g626q56ddt8\",\"bannerImage\":\"vrbqmu7naznndyx8410j8yyp1b7d\",\"synopsis\":\"Set in the glamour of 1950’s post-war London, renowned dressmaker Reynolds Woodcock [Daniel Day-Lewis] and his sister Cyril [Lesley Manville] are at the center of British fashion, dressing royalty, movie stars, heiresses, socialites, debutants and dames with the distinct style of The House of Woodcock. Women come and go through Woodcock’s life, providing the confirmed bachelor with inspiration and companionship, until he comes across a young, strong-willed woman, Alma [Vicky Krieps], who soon becomes a fixture in his life as his muse and lover. Once controlled and planned, he finds his carefully tailored life disrupted by love. With his latest film, Paul Thomas Anderson paints an illuminating portrait both of an artist on a creative journey, and the women who keep his world running. Phantom Thread is Paul Thomas Anderson’s eighth movie, and his second collaboration with Daniel Day-Lewis.\",\"starring\":\"Daniel Day-Lewis, Vicky Krieps, Lesley Manville, Camilla Rutherford, Jane Perry, Ingrid Sophie Schram\",\"directedBy\":\"Paul Thomas Anderson\",\"producedBy\":null,\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":125,\"genre\":null,\"allGenres\":null,\"rating\":\"15\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"xNsiQMeSvMk\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-12-09\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-12-09\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":null,\"tmdbId\":null,\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"230175\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Phantom Thread (2D) [15]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99314099994,\\\"daysShown\\\":140,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Knitflicks\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Knitflicks\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-knitflicks every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-knitflicks showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"463115\",\"time\":\"2026-12-09T20:00:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":1,\"screenId\":\"442\",\"seatsRemaining\":59,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser knitflicks\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"34696\",\"name\":\"Small Things Like These\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"small-things-like-these\",\"posterImage\":\"u2wucbmuvplc5ddvlg6hkeacs80a\",\"bannerImage\":\"neyly3z6anqz3mbk9yr342820p0e\",\"synopsis\":\"Oscar® winner Cillian Murphy delivers a stunning performance as devoted father Bill Furlong in this film based on the best-selling novel of the same name by Claire Keegan. While working as a coal merchant to support his family, he discovers disturbing secrets kept by the local convent — and uncovers truths of his own — forcing him to confront his past and the complicit silence of a small Irish town controlled by the Catholic Church.\",\"starring\":\"Cillian Murphy, Emily Watson, Michelle Fairley\",\"directedBy\":\"Tim Mielants\",\"producedBy\":\"Matt Damon, Cillian Murphy, Alan Moloney, Jeff Robinov, Catherine Magee, Drew Vinton\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":98,\"genre\":\"Drama\",\"allGenres\":\"Drama\",\"rating\":\"12A\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"PBJ3zgH4pGM\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2024-11-01\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-12-10\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":2.9813,\"tmdbId\":\"1102493\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"421702\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"Small Things Like These (2D) [12A]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99314199994,\\\"daysShown\\\":141,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Books On Film\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"5.1\\\",\\\"4K\\\",\\\"Laser\\\",\\\"Ad Free\\\",\\\"Books On Film\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-51 some-showings-4k some-showings-laser some-showings-ad-free some-showings-books-on-film every-showings-51 every-showings-4k every-showings-laser every-showings-ad-free every-showings-books-on-film showing-status-on-sale\\\"}\",\"showings\":[{\"id\":\"397546\",\"time\":\"2026-12-10T19:45:00Z\",\"ticketsSold\":3,\"screenId\":\"440\",\"seatsRemaining\":98,\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"classes\\\":\\\"51 4k laser ad-free books-on-film\\\"}\"}]},{\"id\":\"39091\",\"name\":\"West Side Story\",\"showingStatus\":\"On Sale\",\"urlSlug\":\"west-side-story\",\"posterImage\":\"iq7sa63ssdxnlma2lgngf9wv8iip\",\"bannerImage\":\"kl6wgod8carnf5a7jwx60l3nkbjf\",\"synopsis\":\"\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003eCo-directed by Robert Wise and Jerome Robbins and starring\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003eNatalie Wood and Richard Beymer. This is Romeo and Juliet, with music by Leonard Bernstein and lyrics by Stephen Sondheim, re-imagined in terms of New York gang warfare with electrifying choreography.\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003eAbout the season:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003ePeople often say that if Shakespeare were alive today he would be writing for the movies. What is startling is how often, since the beginnings of cinema, his plays have been adapted for the screen.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003e\\u003cbr\\u003e\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003cspan style=\\\"font-size: 14px;\\\"\\u003eFollowing a highly successful season devoted to the work of Harold Pinter, Chiswick Cinema now focuses on the infinite variety of filmed Shakespeare and will accompany four major screenings with talks, supplementary showings and celebrity interviews.\\u003c/span\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\",\"starring\":\"Natalie Wood, Richard Beymer, Russ Tamblyn\",\"directedBy\":\"Robert Wise, Jerome Robbins\",\"producedBy\":\"\",\"searchTerms\":\"\",\"duration\":152,\"genre\":\"Crime\",\"allGenres\":\"Crime, Drama, Romance\",\"rating\":\"PG\",\"trailerYoutubeId\":\"NF1L3NorO3E\",\"trailerVideo\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"1961-12-13\",\"dateOfFirstShowing\":\"2026-12-13\",\"tmdbPopularityScore\":3.075,\"tmdbId\":\"1725\",\"dcmEdiMovieId\":\"338692\",\"dcmEdiMovieName\":\"West Side Story (1961) (60Th Anniversary) (2D) [PG]\",\"siteId\":\"170\",\"titleClassId\":\"419\",\"displayMetaData\":\"{\\\"magicSortValue\\\":99314499995,\\\"daysShown\\\":144,\\\"nowPlayingOrHasPlayed\\\":false,\\\"someShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Q\\\\u0026A\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Shakespeare on Screen\\\"],\\\"everyShowingsBadges\\\":[\\\"Q\\\\u0026A\\\",\\\"Intro\\\",\\\"Shakespeare on Screen\\\"],\\\"leavesSoon\\\":false,\\\"lastDayTomorrow\\\":false,\\\"lastDayToday\\\":false,\\\"classes\\\":\\\"title-class-classics some-showings-qa some-showings-intro some-showings-shakespeare-on-screen every-showings-qa every-showings-intro every-showings-shake